    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0143" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2367</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-03-31T00:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 31, 1916, midnight</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There is much uneasiness among the native population here and it is reported that
                    certain troops are ready to revolt. I am taking every precaution but do not
                    think that harm will befall foreigners as the mutiny, if begun, will be innately
                    a political demonstration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
